WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.140
Hi, welcome back.

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:04.910
Certainly glad you could join me today.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.530
I brought my little friend Hoot on one more time

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.370
so you could see him.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:09.370
We've got so many cards,

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.610
and people have called asking about him.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.070
I just wanted to show him again.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.210
He's a little baby owl,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.220
and he's one of the cutest little devils.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.040
See if we can get him to put his wings out here.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.090
Look at there, isn't he beautiful?

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.290
He's about three weeks old now,

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:25.750
two and a half weeks or so,

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.680
and very, very cute.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:29.960
Yeah, you're going to...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.700
talk a little bit, he really is a beauty.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:35.170
I am so fascinated with these little creatures,

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:38.780
and I hope you are too, because I like to show them to you.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.080
Look right up there, you see?

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.600
There we go, and he's just nothing but down.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.920
As I mentioned earlier, him and I have the same hairdresser.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.150
We both got the fuzz top up here.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.930
Okay, tell you what, time for us to go to work.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.590
So I'm gonna set him down, I'll have them run all the colors

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.090
across the screen that you need to paint along with me today,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.580
and we'll get started.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.740
No, I'll set him right over here in his little basket.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.320
Now this son of a gun has some talons on him

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.120
that's just unreal, even at his age.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.580
They must be a half an inch long, and he will get you.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.120
Not on purpose, but that's just what happens.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.680
Tell you what, I've got something

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.800
a little different up here today.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.380
I've had so many letters come in from people

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.960
who like to paint on wooden objects,

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.040
asking if this technique can be done on wood.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.300
I thought today I would show that.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.260
So what I've done here is taken just a piece of plywood,

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.980
and I've just sort of cut out a little design.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.060
And when you're at home you can cut out any design that you want.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.580
One thing you might do is, when you cut it, cut it at an angle.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.160
So this slants outward on the sides, all the way around.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.220
And then maybe paint out a flat black when you're all done.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:44.580
And it's like a frame.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:51.520
So I've cut this out and then I've covered it with a thin coat of white gesso.

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:55.820
Let that dry, then I've just put a thin even coat of liquid white over it.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:56.980
So it's ready to go.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.660
Basically it's the same way we do a canvas on its own wood.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.040
And I thought today we'd just do a very simple

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.140
little painting just to show you how it works.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.980
We'll start out with a little touch of alizarin crimson

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.160
on the two-inch brush.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.790
Just pull a little bit of the color out,

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.830
small amount, tap it into the bristles.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.040
And let's put a little pink in this sky,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.640
maybe right in here.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.190
There we are.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.200
Now we don't want to set this sky on fire.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.700
All we want to do is put a little pinkish glow in the sky.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.880
We're just making little criss-cross strokes.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.160
But now in yours, you can make it as bright

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.900
or as dull as you want.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.870
It's up to you, totally up to you.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.480
Anything that you want to do.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.210
There, maybe a little more right in here.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.110
Now then, without cleaning the brush,

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.100
I'm gonna go right into a small amount of the phthalo blue.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.200
Phthalo blue.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.400
And just tap a little into the bristles.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:56.510
Very easy.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:58.950
Let's go right back up here.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:02:59.980
Now right at the top.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.180
at the very top, still using our little criss-cross strokes.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.340
Just begin putting in a happy little sky.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:10.380
There we are.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.610
Just let it blend right on down to the pink.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.650
Now painting on this wood is very nice,

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.240
it's very solid, and it works well.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.440
You can also paint on masonite,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.980
if it has a coat or two of gesso on it.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.120
We'll just bring some little streaky things in here

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.220
just by tapping, then giving it a little blend.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:29.980
You can make all kinds of...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.720
kinds of little effects, wherever you want them.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.180
As I was saying though, Masonite makes a very nice

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.100
surface to paint on.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.520
The only thing that's really different about wood

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.100
or Masonite is when you're using the knife.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.820
This is very hard, there's no give to it.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.980
Unlike canvas, when you paint with a knife on canvas,

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.340
it gives, it bends to the shape of the knife.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.440
This has no bend to it, of course.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:56.190
Maybe we'll put a happy little cloud in there.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:58.330
What the heck, let's go into titanium white.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:03:59.790
We'll use the old fan brush.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.060
Just titanium white, be right back, don't go away.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:05.670
A little bit of bright red in it.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.040
We'll just sparkle this up a little.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.400
Okay, let's go up here.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:14.290
Maybe in our world, there lives a happy little cloud here.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.660
And you could put them anywhere you want,

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.610
just any old place.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.910
Tiny little circles, tiny little circles.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:25.890
I'm gonna brighten him up just a wee bit.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.340
I hope you enjoy seeing Hoot and all the other

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:34.520
little creatures that I bring you.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.870
They are really very special to me,

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.820
and they're some of the best friends in the world.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.360
I love little animals, all kinds of little animals.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:49.430
There, now with a large brush,

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.380
I'm just gonna blend the bottom out,

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.860
just exactly the same way we would do on canvas,

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.510
just like so.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.680
I still have a little squirrel

00:04:58.680 --> 00:04:59.900
that lives with me in my home.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.680
and he lives in a great big cage.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.400
We call it Squirrel Hilton.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:08.350
Boy, that little son of a gun, he is something else.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.770
But he's a little bit too uncontrollable

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.000
to bring on the show.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.060
Maybe I'll take a picture of him

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.740
and show you in one of the next series or something.

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.010
I couldn't keep him still long enough

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:18.750
to bring him out here.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.730
He lives in Florida.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.880
I have a home in Florida, and the squirrel stays there.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:26.200
He knows about this cold weather.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.660
Okay, maybe, tell you what.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.180
Let's just take us a little black,

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.660
a little Prussian blue, a little crimson,

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.580
a little Van Dyke brown, what the heck, just dark colors.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:41.650
Pull it out very flat.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.730
Really get tough with it when you're pulling it out like this.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.130
Pull it out as flat as you can get it.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.280
Go straight down with the knife, touch, and just pull it.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.700
This knife has a straight edge on it,

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.440
so it's very easy to load a roll of paint

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.270
right out on the edge of the blade, okay?

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.980
And maybe, in our world here, they're lit.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.580
a happy little mountain.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.790
We'll do this just like we do when we're painting on wood.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:10.040
But you can hear the difference, of course,

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:15.850
and really push that color in.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.920
There's a little bump there wherever you want it,

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.840
just any kind of mountain that you want.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.540
And maybe where you live, or maybe in your painting,

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.640
you don't want a mountain.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:29.980
If you don't, leave it.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.470
Just leave it out, just leave it out, there we go.

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.140
Now we'll just take the large brush

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.550
and begin blending that color down.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.410
Because there's liquid white on this wood,

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:46.840
the paint will move, it'll slide, just fantastic.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.140
And these wooden things are pretty in your house,

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.260
or you can paint such things as cabinet doors

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:58.260
or whatever you want, just hang them around the house.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:06:59.520
They're beautiful decorations.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:01.820
and you can cut any shape that you want.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:03.610
I used to live in Alaska,

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.270
for years and years I lived in Alaska,

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.080
and I used to cut out maps of the state of Alaska,

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.680
and onto that then I would paint beautiful scenes,

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.080
and sometimes maybe even mount a little clock

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.420
up here in the corner or something.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.800
You can buy a quartz movement to put on the back

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:18.440
for only a few dollars,

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.090
and you can have a clock here with your painting.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.960
And of course, nobody's interested in selling paintings,

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.160
but if you're looking for that happy buck,

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:29.520
little things like that sometimes sell like hotcakes.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.440
I'm gonna take just straight titanium white

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:35.260
with a little bit of, little tiny bit of bright red in it.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:39.040
Cut off my little roll of paint again, just like before.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:43.300
And let's just go up in here, touch, no pressure.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.620
No pressure at all.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.810
Just let it glide.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:50.710
Soom, make little noises.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:55.030
See, it can just glide right down the side of the mountain.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.850
You can go anywhere that you want to go with it.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:58.290
There's another one.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:05.630
There, barely, barely touching, barely touching.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:13.380
Just caress it, maybe.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.260
Over in here, there's a little bit of light

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:16.980
playing through there.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:21.360
Take some white, we'll put a little bit of blue in it.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.010
A little blue, a little touch of black

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:27.070
just to dull it down a little bit.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:29.770
So we have sort of a blue-gray color.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:33.150
Once again, get our little roll of paint

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.530
right out on the edge of the knife.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.930
Then with that, we'll come right up here, touch,

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:39.960
and follow the mountain right down.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:40.420
Zoom.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.500
No pressure, though.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.770
All you're doing is just allowing the knife to float.

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:48.930
That easy.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:53.060
And it's easier to do it fast than it is to do it slow.

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.760
One of the things we do when we're training instructors,

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:58.700
we have instructors that travel around and teach.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:08:59.960
Well, I train these.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.410
of these instructors, and one of the tests that we give them,

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:06.110
we make them paint very, very fast,

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.780
because you find that they can paint better fast sometimes

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:10.620
than they can slow.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:12.780
When you're doing things like this,

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.560
it's hard to do it slow like this.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:18.650
If you just do it, it happens much faster, much easier,

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:19.850
and the paint breaks better.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.230
By breaking, we mean it has all these little holes in it,

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.680
and you can do that, see?

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:27.820
Anywhere you want a shadow,

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:29.810
you just drop in a little of that blue.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.050
in the opposing or opposite direction.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:35.400
And you can make some mean, rugged looking mountains.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:37.870
With a clean, dry brush,

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.030
I'm just gonna tap the base of this.

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:42.890
Just tap it, like so.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:46.200
Very lightly blend it upward.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.770
By blending upward, all it does is take out

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.880
the little tap marks, brings everything together,

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.330
creates that illusion of mist at the base of your mountain.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.740
Very soft and very delicate.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.540
far away.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:04.040
Over here, you follow these angles.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.980
It's most important when you're doing this tapping

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.310
that you follow the angles in your mountain.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.750
Now take a little more of that blue on my brush,

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:12.430
just tap a little.

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:14.870
And sometimes it's fun just to take this,

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:17.690
and maybe we'll just bring it right on out

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:20.810
and create a whole new plane in the mountain.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.790
All these planes are what create the illusion

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.140
of depth and distance.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.070
Some little shadows back in here.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.390
all kinds of little happy things.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:38.390
There we go, okay.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:40.670
Let me wash the old brush.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.400
Then we wash our brushes, as you know,

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:44.550
with odorless thinner.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.960
Shake it off, beat the devil out of it.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.180
Now I'm just gonna tap this.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.230
Brush beating is so much fun.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.490
Hoot's not too crazy about it though,

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:58.530
it sort of shakes him up.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:10:59.980
He thinks he's next.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.970
There we go.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:07.300
And while I have blue still in that brush chute,

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:10.540
we'll just go right into a little touch of crimson

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:14.330
and come right across here.

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:19.110
Throw in a nice little color, just like so.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.300
A little lavender color in the middle.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:27.670
And we'll go right into a little bit of phthalo blue

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.980
and do the edging.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.960
like so.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.040
We'll just put a little bit of water down here.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:36.640
What the heck.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.700
Once again, this is mixing with the liquid white

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:45.760
and it's very smooth and it just flows.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:48.300
If you had a dry board here that you were trying to paint on,

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.900
you would really be in agony city right now

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.360
and you'd be very unhappy with me.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.380
You'd be calling me names.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.520
Having the liquid white on there.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.380
That's just as slick as it can be.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.750
Your color's continually mixing with it.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:07.070
And all these beautiful things just happen automatically.

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:13.570
Okay, maybe back here we have some little foothills.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:17.200
We'll take, we got some black here,

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:18.660
and a little bit of Prussian blue,

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.460
brown, a little sap green.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.800
Be right back, I'm gonna get a little white.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:29.900
A little bit of white, there we go.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:33.530
Maybe a little more brown.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:35.510
I want to dull that, it's getting a little too bright.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:37.720
Oh, that's nice, that's nice.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:40.160
Tap a little color into the bristles.

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:41.670
Let's go right up here.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:45.020
Now then, maybe back in here,

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:48.020
just live some beautiful little foothills.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.520
All kinds of little trees

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:52.010
that are way back here in the distance.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:55.680
I'm using the brush up like this

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.020
so it makes it look like the tops

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:59.490
of just hundreds and hundreds and hundreds

00:12:59.490 --> 00:12:59.970
of little trees.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.320
trees.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:03.380
