He's sitting right here, there we are.

00:26:37.040 --> 00:26:40.020
Now then, with our knife, just a clean knife,

00:26:40.570 --> 00:26:41.910
we go up here in these dark areas,

00:26:43.270 --> 00:26:45.060
creep in our little sticks, twigs,

00:26:45.460 --> 00:26:46.540
all kinds of little things.

00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:49.510
I'm gonna take a little Van Dyke brown,

00:26:50.100 --> 00:26:52.580
let's go right over here, put in a little bit of land.

00:26:54.230 --> 00:26:56.460
There, look at that, a little brown and white,

00:26:57.590 --> 00:26:58.190
a little highlight.

00:27:00.160 --> 00:27:01.540
A little liquid white on the knife.

00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:02.860
We'll put in a water line.

00:27:03.970 --> 00:27:06.430
Geez, we got that rascal just about finished.

00:27:08.250 --> 00:27:09.690
But I hope this shows you how you can take

00:27:09.690 --> 00:27:12.590
an old piece of plywood and turn it into

00:27:12.590 --> 00:27:16.010
a beautiful, beautiful painting that once again

00:27:16.060 --> 00:27:18.720
makes a fantastic gift to give to loved ones

00:27:18.720 --> 00:27:20.610
or just anybody you're looking for something

00:27:20.610 --> 00:27:21.350
to give for a gift.

00:27:22.140 --> 00:27:23.940
So with that, I think we'll call this one finished

00:27:23.940 --> 00:27:25.450
from all of us here.

00:27:25.720 --> 00:27:27.360
And from Ol' Hoot, I'd like to wish you

00:27:27.360 --> 00:27:29.060
a happy painting and God bless.

